        if (at >= 0) {
            std::cout << "yes at " << at << '\n';
        } else {
            std::cout << "no" << '\n';
        }
    }
    return 0;
}

steps.body:
To count the subarrays that sum to exactly `k`, even with negative numbers, keep a running total. The stretch after some earlier point up to here sums to `total - earlier`, so it equals `k` exactly when an earlier running total was `total - k`. An `unordered_map` counts how many times each running total has appeared:

```cpp
std::vector<int> nums = {1, 2, 3, -2, 2};
int k = 3;
std::unordered_map<long long, int> seen;
seen[0] = 1;                         // the empty prefix, before any number
long long total = 0;
int count = 0;
for (int x : nums) {
    total += x;
    auto it = seen.find(total - k);
    if (it != seen.end()) {
        count += it->second;
    }
    ++seen[total];
}
std::cout << count << '\n';          // 4
```

Look up `total - k` before you count `total` itself, or a `k` of 0 would count an empty stretch. The `seen[0] = 1` entry is for stretches that start at the very first number. `find` reads the map without inserting, and the totals are `long long` because many numbers can add up past 2 billion. One pass with O(1) map operations makes it O(n), where checking every stretch would be O(n^2).

example.code:
#include <iostream>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <vector>

int main() {
    int n = 0;
    std::cin >> n;
    std::vector<int> nums(n);
    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
        std::cin >> nums[i];
    }
    int q = 0;
    std::cin >> q;
    for (int t = 0; t < q; ++t) {
        int k = 0;
        std::cin >> k;
        std::unordered_map<long long, int> seen;
        seen[0] = 1;
        long long total = 0;
        int count = 0;
        for (int x : nums) {
            total += x;
            auto it = seen.find(total - k);
            if (it != seen.end()) {
                count += it->second;
            }
            ++seen[total];
        }
        std::cout << "sum " << k << ": " << count << '\n';
    }
    return 0;
}

